  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `fn[format_node_content]` inside `impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Contents]` in `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` is a valid coverage exception.\n\n- **Form:** It sits on an explicit function with a body. The explanation is in fenced citation commentary, as the built-in requires. It gives a substantive reason, not just difficulty. `Contents` requires a formatter, but the test deliberately uses only outgoing-edge tools. Rendering contents would imply an unwanted content input, so the body is a `panic!` guard that should never run.\n- **Agreement with the source:** In `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`, every scripted agent turn calls `outgoing_edges` or `submit_result`. None calls `read_node`. The test asserts that the dependencies are only `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`. The function is therefore unreachable in this test, as the commentary says.\n- **Other tests:** The claim that other agent tests exercise rendering with explicitly requested contents holds. `Memory`'s `impl[Memory/Contents]/fn[format_node_content]` calls the configurable formatter. Tests such as `node_rendering_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents`, `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` and `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` request contents with `read_node` or `contents_of_current_node`.",
